Relevant tables / columns and how they will be used

pizza_customer_orders  
 • order_id: join‐key to extras / exclusions and the runner tables.  
 • customer_id: required in the final output.  
 • pizza_id: join with pizza_names and pizza_recipes to pick standard recipe.  
 • exclusions: original string column (kept just in case).  
 • extras: original string column (kept just in case).  
 • order_time: (needed only for the GROUP BY requirement).

pizza_get_exclusions  
 • order_id: joins to pizza_customer_orders.  
 • exclusions: single excluded topping_id.  
 • total_exclusions: number of exclusions per row_id (handy check).  
 • row_id: will be reported in the final answer (acts like the “row ID” for every order).

pizza_get_extras  
 • order_id: joins to pizza_customer_orders.  
 • extras: single additional topping_id.  
 • extras_count: number of extras per row_id (handy check).  
 • row_id: same “row ID” as above.

pizza_recipes  
 • pizza_id: joins to pizza_customer_orders.  
 • toppings: comma‑separated list of the standard topping_id’s to start from.

pizza_toppings  
 • topping_id: joins to pizza_recipes / extras / exclusions.  
 • topping_name: human readable ingredient for the final string.  

pizza_names  
 • pizza_id: joins to pizza_customer_orders.  
 • pizza_name: human readable pizza name to put in the beginning of the final string.  

Conditions we will probably need  
 • pizza_names.pizza_id = 1 → always “Meatlovers”; anything else = 2.  
 • Join pizza_get_exclusions and pizza_get_extras on order_id, grouping by row_id.  
 • For each order take recipe_toppings – exclusions + extras.  
 • If the same topping is in the final set more than once ⇒ prefix with ‘2x’.  
 • Alphabetical order of ingredient names when concatenating.  
 • GROUP BY row_id, order_id, pizza_name, order_time.  
 • Final SELECT ordered by row_id ASC.

Ten exploratory SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows)

```sql
-- 1. Distinct pizza ids and names available
SELECT DISTINCT pizza_id, pizza_name
FROM pizza_names
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect all recipes and their raw topping lists
